MONAI (Medical Open Network for AI) Training tutorials
MONAI (Medical Open Network for AI) provides a comprehensive ecosystem of tutorials designed to help you build, train, and deploy medical AI models. 
🚀 Core Learning Resources
Official MONAI Tutorials Repository: The primary source for hands-on learning is the Project-MONAI/tutorials GitHub repository, which contains dozens of Jupyter notebooks for segmentation, classification, and GANs.
NVIDIA MONAI Toolkit: Offers a structured learning experience through five comprehensive modules, covering everything from data labeling to model deployment.
MONAI YouTube Channel: Features recordings of MONAI Bootcamps and technical deep dives into specific tools like MONAI Label. 

🛠️ Key Training Pipelines
Beginner: MedNIST Classification: A "Hello World" style tutorial using a small dataset of medical images (X-rays, MRI, CT) to teach basic MONAI transforms and training loops.
Intermediate: 3D Spleen Segmentation: A step-by-step guide to training a 3D UNet model using the Medical Segmentation Decathlon dataset.
Advanced: MONAI Bundle: Learn to use standardized config-based workflows that package models, metadata, and scripts for reproducibility. 

🔍 Specialized Tooling Tutorials
MONAI Label: Tutorials on how to use AI-assisted labeling in tools like 3D Slicer to reduce data annotation time.
Auto3DSeg: Learn how to use AutoML for 3D medical imaging, which automatically tunes hyperparameters and architectures for your specific dataset.
Federated Learning: Examples of using MONAI with NVIDIA FLARE or Flower to train models across multiple institutions without sharing raw data. 

